WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.420
Bad dad or unreliable narrator? Mistreatin’&nbsp;
Missy or sheer child neglect? Young Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.840
isn’t the childlike fairytale you’d&nbsp;
think it is; and for a lot of fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.020
the controversy just stirs the&nbsp;
pot for a Big Bang in the making!

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.200
Most fans can forgive Young Sheldon's producers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.800
for casting actor Lance Barber as&nbsp;
the character George Cooper Sr.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.020
after he played Leonard's bully Jimmy Speckerman&nbsp;
in Season 5 of The Big Bang Theory. But usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.340
they still can't get over the "bad dad"&nbsp;
narrative perpetuated in the original show.

00:00:29.736 --> 00:00:37.623
"My father used to say that a woman is like&nbsp;
an egg-salad sandwich on a warm Texas day."

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:41.820
During its early seasons, Young Sheldon&nbsp;
established George Cooper as a caring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.200
and thoughtful father and husband. Sure, he&nbsp;
doesn't always get it right and is tough on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.520
the kids sometimes, but it's a far cry from&nbsp;
the skeet-obsessed redneck described on The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.260
Big Bang Theory. Barber's performance has&nbsp;
prompted many fans online to debate if and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.160
when we’ll see the real George Cooper&nbsp;
emerge, with one Reddit user claiming,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.960
"That has been one thing that has irked me&nbsp;
to no end. George Cooper Sr's character is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.920
such a well written one. Most of the scenes&nbsp;
with him are my favorites from the show."

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.960
Another fan suggested that Young Sheldon viewers&nbsp;
are seeing the true version of George, speculating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.060
that Sheldon on The Big Bang Theory is just an&nbsp;
unreliable narrator. He often recalls events from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.680
his childhood without having all the facts, and&nbsp;
even over-exaggerates aspects of other characters.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.940
Some Young Sheldon fans take issue&nbsp;
with how Raegan Revord's character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.980
Missy is treated — or rather mistreated —&nbsp;
by her family. One Reddit fan commented,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.280
"I don't like that their parents and&nbsp;
Meemaw heard Missy say she doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.120
have anyone on her team and yet they still&nbsp;
didn't make more of an effort with her."

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.160
This moment takes place in Episode 5 of Season&nbsp;
2, while Sheldon and Missy are being evaluated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.480
in a twin study. Missy, who’s observed&nbsp;
by Dr. Thorpe as being very perceptive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.740
says her perception comes from being on&nbsp;
her own a lot. She explains that her mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.220
dad, and Meemaw are often busy&nbsp;
tending to Georgie or Sheldon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.380
so she has no one supporting her. Shocked by&nbsp;
this realization, they do initially start to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.580
more of an effort to be there for her, first by&nbsp;
letting her pick the restaurant on the way home.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:11.040
However, the Coopers' neglect of Missy largely&nbsp;
continues, giving Revord some big scenes in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.320
Season 6. As another Reddit user pointed out, her&nbsp;
family just continues to prove that they aren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.840
really on her team, leaving Missy to feel like the&nbsp;
forgotten member of the family. This is especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.520
true when she misses the birth of her niece, and&nbsp;
in the following episode, she runs away from home.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.980
When the series kicks off, Sheldon's maternal&nbsp;
grandmother Connie Tucker nicknamed Meemaw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:37.260
hasn't moved on from the death of her husband four&nbsp;
years earlier. As Season 1 continues, she starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:42.060
to form a connection with Sheldon's professor&nbsp;
and friend, John Sturgis. By the season finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.200
they've made their relationship official with&nbsp;
Sheldon's first-ever relationship contract.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:47.985
"Please sign and date."&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.580
"You know, Seldon. I'm a notary, if that helps."
"Just when I thought you couldn't get cooler."

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.000
Young Sheldon fans were thrilled&nbsp;
to see this relationship blossom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.560
with a user on Reddit commenting,

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.520
"John and Connie are so full of love&nbsp;
and understanding [...] Kudos to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.680
makers for hitting the sweetest spot on the show!"

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.840
Another user agreed, commenting,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.740
"Can we please have John and Connie&nbsp;
forever? They are so adorable together."

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.720
However, John and Connie's relationship only&nbsp;
lasted one season, with them splitting after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.220
John's mental breakdown at the end of Season&nbsp;
2. Even though Connie has since dated Dale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.780
Ballard — played by Craig T. Nelson — Young&nbsp;
Sheldon fans are still seemingly unable to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.557
get over her split with John, with many&nbsp;
still hoping they'll get back together.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.780
Emily Osment's character, Mandy McAllister, has&nbsp;
been part of Young Sheldon since she met Georgie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.100
midway through Season 5. Their relationship&nbsp;
quickly developed and by the time the season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:42.660
was out, Mandy was pregnant. However, before&nbsp;
they discovered they're going to be parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.800
their romance abruptly ended when&nbsp;
Georgie admitted he wasn't 21 years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.620
but actually 17. Early in Season 6, Georgie&nbsp;
tries to get back into Mandy's good graces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.620
doing everything he can to make&nbsp;
her pregnancy more comfortable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.460
They continue to learn about one other,&nbsp;
often acting like any dating couple.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.320
But when Mandy and Georgie bring the newborn&nbsp;
Constance Cooper — nicknamed CeeCee — home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.680
from the hospital, they're still not&nbsp;
a functioning couple no matter how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.580
devoted they are to their child. Although&nbsp;
Osment is a welcome addition to the cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:16.740
many fans want the show to move on from this&nbsp;
"situationship," with one Reddit user commenting,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.340
"This whole thing with Mandy and&nbsp;
Georgie is quite ridiculous. Can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.080
they just have them officially together already?"

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:26.580
Not all fans are rooting for the pair, with&nbsp;
some suggesting that Georgie would be better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.380
off without Mandy. But either way, it seems as&nbsp;
if things are finally moving in some direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.404
initiated by Georgie's surprise&nbsp;
proposal late in Season 6.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:40.200
When viewers first meet Mckenna Grace's&nbsp;
Paige in Season 2, she's a sweet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.880
gifted child who eventually takes a dark&nbsp;
turn after her parents' divorce. By Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.160
it's clear this child prodigy is struggling.

00:04:47.401 --> 00:04:54.541
"Everything that used to seem&nbsp;
important to me just doesn't anymore."

00:04:54.541 --> 00:05:00.180
By Season 6, Paige has taken on a new title of the&nbsp;
underage party girl. As a Reddit user pointed out,

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:03.240
"Each guest appearance has shown&nbsp;
her progressively getting worse."

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.840
Paige once admitted to Sheldon that&nbsp;
she wasn't being taken seriously as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:11.220
a young woman in science, and ultimately&nbsp;
dropped out of college. Paige loses her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.640
way and winds up back at East Texas&nbsp;
Tech, with one Redditor observing,

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.600
"Now she's just going off with a nasty&nbsp;
attitude and then getting drunk at parties,"

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.660
Some Young Sheldon fans were&nbsp;
completely shocked by this;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.860
suggesting that her actions are an obvious&nbsp;
cry for help, with one user commenting,

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.580
"The show won't go that deep, but&nbsp;
I wonder if she lived to see her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.460
20s. It looks like her teenage&nbsp;
years are going to be dark."

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.040
The world isn't always fair and Young Sheldon&nbsp;
proves it in Season 5 when Mary is fired from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:43.440
her job at the church. Matt Hobby's Pastor Jeff&nbsp;
brings Mary, George and Pastor Rob — played by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.920
Dan Byrd — into his office after the&nbsp;
congregation learns that Georgie is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:51.780
having a baby out of wedlock. He beats around the&nbsp;
bush before telling Mary that she needs to leave.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.840
Although she quickly finds a job&nbsp;
working at the bowling alley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.340
audiences criticized Pastor Jeff for&nbsp;
firing her. One Reddit user commented,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.780
"I feel like Jeff is a hypocrite. Being&nbsp;
divorced is enough to disqualify him even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.320
being a Baptist pastor. One would&nbsp;
think he'd be more sympathetic."

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:12.300
Other fans agreed that, while wrong, Pastor&nbsp;
Jeff was pressured into it to save face with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:17.640
other members of the church. But this storyline is&nbsp;
probably not over yet. When we see Mary in The Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.660
Bang Theory she's still involved with the church,&nbsp;
so maybe Pastor Jeff will make things right.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.540
Of course, many of the biggest storylines in Young&nbsp;
Sheldon are dictated by The Big Bang Theory. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.920
that looms over the whole series is the death of&nbsp;
George, which is supposed to occur when Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.720
and Missy are 14 years old. With George having&nbsp;
two heart attacks in the first five seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.260
Young Sheldon has been setting the tone&nbsp;
for this storyline for a long time.

00:06:40.677 --> 00:06:45.287
"Enough questions. He's a fat, middle-aged&nbsp;
man with chest pains. Do something!"

00:06:45.287 --> 00:06:48.720
By Season 6, the twins are nearing that&nbsp;
age and some fans are bracing for impact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.334
with a Twitter user commenting,

00:06:50.431 --> 00:06:53.520
"It occurs to me that the show has&nbsp;
to have George die before the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.380
and I don't think I'm emotionally ready for that."

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.760
Other fans are hoping to avoid the heartbreak,&nbsp;
convinced by the differences in George's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.260
character between Young Sheldon and The Big Bang&nbsp;
Theory that his death won't happen. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:08.580
writer and executive producer Steve Holland&nbsp;
told TVLine that the show would be largely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.340
sticking to the canonical events&nbsp;
laid out in The Big Bang Theory.

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:16.680
Some Young Sheldon fans have always been critical&nbsp;
of our protagonist, favoring other characters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:22.200
storylines, but now — in Season 6 — some think&nbsp;
he's become completely irrelevant. While the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.400
young genius furthers his education at East&nbsp;
Texas Tech, and works on his database project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.740
some viewers suspect that there's no more room for&nbsp;
Sheldon's development. A Twitter user commented,

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.400
"The worst, least likable, and&nbsp;
uninteresting character on Young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.900
Sheldon is Sheldon. And it's not the&nbsp;
actor's fault. Iain's Sheldon cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.840
grow beyond the point at which we&nbsp;
first saw the character in BBT."

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.700
In a Reddit thread discussing Sheldon's&nbsp;
lack of a solid storyline, one user said.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:51.360
"Now it feels forced and weird. The&nbsp;
other characters have storylines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.380
that grow and move along. Sheldon's&nbsp;
academics have just become boring."

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.180
Another user agreed, adding,

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.060
"They're seriously going to have to&nbsp;
figure out where they want to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.860
his character by the end of the seventh season."

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:06.600
George and Mary don't have the perfect marriage,&nbsp;
but their hearts usually are in the right places.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:11.580
However, there are some things that Mary can't&nbsp;
always get from George — like deep conversation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:17.460
As a result, she's grown closer to Pastor Rob;&nbsp;
her close friend, confidant, and smoking buddy.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:20.880
"What's going on here?"
"Uh, praying. We're praying."&nbsp;

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:21.780
"Just praying."

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.740
While it's pretty clear that the youth&nbsp;
pastor wants more than a platonic friendship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.560
and Mary's been fantasizing&nbsp;
about being together with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.460
nothing has actually happened between&nbsp;
the pair. And some fans are angry over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:36.180
how seemingly ridiculous this storyline&nbsp;
is, with one Twitter user commenting,

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:40.680
"The Young Sheldon plot [with] Mary being accused&nbsp;
of cheating with Pastor Rob [...] deal with being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:45.000
thrown out of her church and maybe have one (1)&nbsp;
friend makes me want to put my tv through a wall."

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.440
Other fans on Reddit claimed that they couldn't&nbsp;
see Mary cheating on George, believing that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:54.359
show is unnecessarily building up her possible&nbsp;
fling with Rob only for dramatic effect.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.980
Sheldon explains in The Big Bang Theory that he&nbsp;
once walked in on his father with another woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:03.300
but some Young Sheldon fans can't seem to get&nbsp;
over the storyline in which George cheats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:07.740
This is since it doesn't fit with the character&nbsp;
they've gotten to know. One viewer commented,

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:12.180
"The Mary and George parts are disappointing.&nbsp;
I hate it that their marriage is bad that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.260
are looking at others. Sad. I liked it much&nbsp;
better when they loved only each other."

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:20.160
Some audiences think Geroge's budding&nbsp;
affair with Brenda Sparks — played by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.960
Melissa Peterman — is just an attempt to stay&nbsp;
faithful to The Big Bang Theory. One viewer said,

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.220
"No reason to ruin a good show trying to be&nbsp;
faithful to another show that's off the air."

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.860
How far George has taken this budding affair with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:36.300
Brenda is unclear, but while they're at&nbsp;
the hospital in Episode 14 of Season 6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.960
they exchange banter which seems&nbsp;
to suggest some form of intimacy.

00:09:40.422 --> 00:09:44.974
"I did not give you a heart attack."
"You gave me something."&nbsp;

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:45.780
"Well."

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:50.340
In the episode "A Launch Party and a Whole&nbsp;
Human Being" — moments after that hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:54.240
scene between George and Brenda —&nbsp;
Mary enters with Pastor Rob in tow.

00:09:54.334 --> 00:09:59.614
"I hear we're having a baby. What? Did I miss it?"

00:09:59.614 --> 00:10:04.680
However, nobody is particularly focused on&nbsp;
the laboring mother at that moment. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.260
with Mary catching on that&nbsp;
George is Brenda's mystery man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:11.580
and George thinking that Mary and Pastor Rob were&nbsp;
doing more than just grabbing lunch for hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:16.140
their relationship reaches a breaking&nbsp;
point. Speaking to TVLine, executive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:20.220
producer Steve Holland explained why this was&nbsp;
the perfect time for this to come to a head,

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.640
"We didn't want to do the traditional&nbsp;
'you're in the delivery room and she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:28.080
panting' episode [...] it just seemed like a great&nbsp;
way to have these stories all crash together."

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:32.760
Some viewers think the cheating storylines are a&nbsp;
bit ridiculous, and agree that the birth of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:37.320
granddaughter is neither the time nor the place&nbsp;
to get into them. One Twitter user commented,

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.940
"Mandy's mom is the worst but she has&nbsp;
a point. Mandy is in labor but the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.960
real family she has at the moment would rather&nbsp;
fight over their crushes than check on her."

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:51.060
If Georgie's situation with Mandy is anything&nbsp;
to go by, it's clear he's willing to lie to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:55.800
get a girl. In Season 2, Georgie meets and&nbsp;
starts dating Veronica — played by Isabel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:00.540
May. But after an intense make-out session,&nbsp;
Veronica decides to change gears and devote her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:06.234
life to Christianity. So in order to keep dating&nbsp;
Veronica, Georgie pretends that he's also devout.

00:11:06.234 --> 00:11:08.880
"Georgie, if you want to be&nbsp;
a good Christian, maybe you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:12.360
should stop lying through your teeth."
"Just be happy I brushed them, okay?"

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:16.200
But their relationship ends shortly&nbsp;
after, with Veronica last seen across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:19.560
a restaurant when Gerogie's on a date&nbsp;
with his new girlfriend. Although she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.160
only appeared for a handful of episodes in&nbsp;
the first three seasons of Young Sheldon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.660
fans enjoyed Veronica's transformation into a&nbsp;
responsible young woman and were disappointed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.720
in her abrupt departure. On Reddit, a user posted,

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:34.200
"Is anyone else annoyed at the&nbsp;
removal of Veronica? She was one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:37.440
of my favorite characters and I loved her&nbsp;
relationship with everyone on the show."

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:42.660
Several other fans agreed, noting that Veronica's&nbsp;
storyline never came to a satisfying conclusion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:46.922
Others are hoping that she'll return and&nbsp;
reunite with Georgie, with a viewer commenting,

00:11:46.922 --> 00:11:49.080
"Veronica seemed like a sweetheart and I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.660
she'd [have] been a better fit&nbsp;
for Georgie instead of Mandy."

